00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You've known Poehler
for a long time.

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
You met Amy Poehler
back in Chicago.

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:03.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
What was your
first meeting like?

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:07.140
-Well, one of my good friend
named Ragsdale lived with --

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm so glad you have
a friend named Ragsdale.

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:11.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Ragsdale. And he's just wha
you would think.

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:15.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, Ragsdale gave me my firs
Neil Gaiman comic book.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:18.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, there you go.
That's a classic Ragsdale move

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:19.886 line:92%
-Ragsdale is like, "You know

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:22.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
you can clean the resin
out of that thing."

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:25.592 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And he had all the tips.

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:27.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
We all need a Ragsdale.

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:30.930
You're lucky.
You had a sensei and a Ragsdale.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Totally.
-Yeah.

00:00:32.399 --> 00:00:35.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Ragsdale lived in a house
with Matt Besser,

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:39.572
one of the founders of
Upright Citizens Brigade.

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:42.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, so, Amy and I met
at parties

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:44.377 line:92%
over there, making mischief.

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:48.448
And we did -- We recognize
one another in a sort of

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:52.719 size:78% position:39%
sibling way of like,
"Hey, you know, like,

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:54.587 size:78% position:39%
you're a class clown,
I'm a class clown."

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:56.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she would always
just punch me.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:01:00.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like, "Yeah,
I've been friends with her

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:01.127 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
for a long time.

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:03.229 line:92%
She punches me when I see her.

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:04.697 line:92%
-And then, of course, you --

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:05.565 line:92%
As we've already mentioned

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:07.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Parks and Recreation,"
Ron Swanson.

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:09.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
To finish up here,
how do you think Ron Swanson

00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:12.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
would be handling
the coronavirus panic?

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:17.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't think he would
necessarily notice.

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:20.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
But if he did, I mean,
Leslie would probably send him

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:22.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
